# Implementation Plan - Minimalist Sidebar Refresh

## Goal
Redesign the Sidebar to be "invisible" until needed, ultra-minimal, and non-blocking. The current version is too heavy and cluttered.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I am proposing to switch from **Boxy Buttons** to a **Clean List** design. No borders, no heavy highlights—just text and subtle hover effects. I will also make the sidebar slightly narrower and more translucent.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] [Sidebar.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/components/Sidebar.tsx)
- **Narrower Width**: Reduce from `280px` to `230px`.
- **Minimalist List**: Remove boxes/borders from lesson and step items. Use a single vertical line for the active step.
- **Improved Header**: Fix alignment of the "Curriculum" title and X button.
- **Glassmorphism**: Increase transparency and blur for a lighter "floating" feel.

### [Style] [index.css](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/index.css)
- **Update `.nav-item`**: Remove base borders and heavy backgrounds.
- **Refine `.sidebar-shelf`**: Adjust shadow and backdrop filter.

### [Component] [Player.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/MathLessonVisualiser/src/components/Player.tsx)
- **Auto-Close**: Ensure the sidebar closes immediately upon selecting a step to clear the view.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
- Verify the sidebar feels "lighter" and less intrusive.
- Verify clicking a step closes the sidebar and reveals the visualization.
- Verify text is legible against the blurred background.
